/-! # Actual categorical foundation for the Picard associator obstruction

The scalar defect is extracted from actual module natural isomorphisms by
the component density/Schur theorem. A bifunctor and an actual natural
triple comparison determine all twenty-one five-input associator moves.
Naturality proves the three interchange squares; cancellation of the two
six-step paths proves the four-variable cocycle equation. No pentagon or
scalar-cocycle certificate is an input.

This generic foundation does not construct the balanced product
equivalences of graph module components, or identify the products with
chosen group-indexed components. Those actual product constructions are
needed to instantiate the obstruction for the Picard action in JF §2.3.
-/
